# Extra egress allowlist for the Rocket.Chat monorepo, merged into the firewall's
# list for workspaces on this profile. Hostnames or CIDRs, `#` comments.
# Takes effect on a container restart — no rebuild. See ../../allowed-domains.

# --- The stacks this profile talks to -----------------------------------------
#
# Belt and braces, and a record of what this profile talks to. The firewall
# already accepts every network the container is attached to, in both directions
# (see ../../scripts/claude-code/init-firewall.sh), and both of these arrive that
# way — so neither line is what makes them reachable any more. They are kept
# because the CIDRs are pinned on the other side and this is where a reader looks
# for them; keep each in sync with the compose file named beside it.
#
# The shared MongoDB — containers/local-mongo/docker-compose.yml. Without a route
# to it, every connection to mongo:27017 fails and the server never boots.
172.31.0.0/24
# The observability stack — containers/observability/docker-compose.yml. Listed
# for Prometheus's scrape of port 9458, which is this profile's. The network
# itself is not this profile's: ../../scripts/ensure-observability.sh attaches
# every container to it, and ../../scripts/claude-code/allowed-domains records
# the same CIDR for the OTLP push going the other way.
172.29.0.0/24

